<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan money and bond markets closed for holiday.</title>
<headline>Taiwan money and bond markets closed for holiday.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-12-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's money and bond markets are closed on Wednesday due to a national holiday. they will reopen on Thursday.</p>
<p>On Tuesday, the overnight interbank rate ended at 5.039 percent against Monday's 4.958 close, with 30-day commercial paper at 4.95-5.00 percent against 5.00.</p>
<p>In the bond market, the 10-year 86/4 bond yield was at 6.1000 percent against 6.0950.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (5080815)</p>
</text>
